            <ArticleTitle>The worst headache ever. 1. Ominous causes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-6, 103-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Headache is always a challenging diagnostic exercise but is especially so in patients who have &quot;the worst headache ever.&quot; Such a headache should never be automatically dismissed as merely a severe but benign one. A thorough history and careful physical examination are necessary to find evidence of serious disease. If such evidence is present, immediate, aggressive, and thorough evaluation are essential to avoid severe consequences.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
